<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6725" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Căpys</span></b> ,
		yos, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κάπυς</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Son of Assaracus</i>, <i>and father of
				Anchises</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. F. 4,
			34</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A companion of Æneas</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 1,
				183</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 35</span></i>; <i><span class="en">9, 576</span></i>; 10, 145
			Serv.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A king of Alba</i>, <i>in Latium</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Ov. M. 14, 613 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 1, 3,
			8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 6,
			768</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>A king of Capua</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 4, 37,
				1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Serv. ad Verg. A. 1,
			242</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
